4. Bundled and fetched data

Model price catalog. service/src/main/resources/model-pricing/ holds a snapshot
of the community-maintained price list in the repository Wei-Shaw/model-price-repo
(https://github.com/Wei-Shaw/model-price-repo), which its maintainers license
under the MIT License. The file follows the format of the LiteLLM model price
list (https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm, MIT License), which is credited here as
the format and likely upstream of that data. The prices are vendor list prices
as collected by that community catalog, not data supplied by the vendors. Unless
STARRY_MODEL_PRICING_REMOTE_REFRESH_ENABLED is set to false, the service
refreshes the catalog from that repository at run time. See
service/src/main/resources/model-pricing/README.md for the snapshot's details.

Model ranking. service/src/main/resources/model-ranking/ holds small factual
snapshots of two public leaderboards: ProgramBench (https://programbench.com/)
and the Terminal-Bench 3.0 leaderboard published at https://www.frontierbench.ai/.
Each snapshot records its source address. The scores and model names belong to
their publishers. By default the service refreshes them at run time from the
files in https://github.com/StaR4y/ai-benchmark-ranking (the
STARRY_MODEL_RANKING_* settings in service/src/main/resources/application.yml
and docker-compose.yml change or switch off that refresh).

News. The console's news page shows items that the service fetches at run time
from the API of https://aihot.news. No news content is bundled with the
software, and the items belong to their publishers.


