6. Mihomo (optional, not distributed)

Starry API can route traffic through Mihomo (the Clash.Meta core,
https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo), which is licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3. Mihomo is optional and Starry API does not include,
bundle or distribute it: no Mihomo binary or container image is part of the
source tree, the executable jar, the deployment bundle or any release file of
this project. When the optional egress component is deployed (the "mihomo"
profile of the Docker Compose files; the installer scripts/install-server.sh
deploys it idle on a fresh install unless ENABLE_MIHOMO=false), Docker pulls the
image metacubex/mihomo from its registry onto the server as a separate container.
It communicates with Starry API only over a local network connection, as a
separate program. Its own license (GPL-3.0) governs that image. The file
docker/egress/mihomo-entrypoint.sh and the "mihomo" service in the Compose files
are Starry API's own and are licensed like the rest of Starry API (AGPL-3.0-only),
not under the license of Mihomo.
